### `DiagnosticDump: gated message-array dumps for content-extraction analysis`

The `--diagnostic-dump` flag (`RouterConfig.DiagnosticDump`) writes the full
`messages` array to `/tmp/discursive-msgdump-<requestID>.json` whenever content
extraction from the last user message returns empty (`stripped_len == 0`).
This only happens when the last message is entirely Cursor XML boilerplate or
the message role is not `user`/`developer` (e.g. tool-result rounds).

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Flag | `--diagnostic-dump` (CLI), `DiagnosticDump bool` (RouterConfig) |
| Default | `false` (off) — must be explicitly enabled |
| Trigger | `stripped_len == 0` (content extraction produced nothing) |
| Output | `/tmp/discursive-msgdump-<requestID>.json` (full `messages` array, indented JSON) |
| Cleanup | `/tmp/` is automatically cleaned on macOS reboot and by Linux `tmpfiles.d` |
| Separation | Gated on `DiagnosticDump`, NOT on `Enabled`. Dumps can fire even when the smart router is disabled, and remain silent even when the router is enabled unless the diagnostic flag is also set. |

